WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.935
Modern expertise is often distributed.

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:07.808
A team may hold more capability than any one individual because knowledge is spread across people,

00:00:07.808 --> 00:00:09.643
documentation, tools, automation, and routines.

00:00:09.643 --> 00:00:12.212
Shared mental models help the group coordinate.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:15.516
Handoffs help expertise move across time and role boundaries.

00:00:15.516 --> 00:00:20.287
Documentation makes important reasoning visible instead of trapping it inside one person's memory.

00:00:20.287 --> 00:00:25.059
Tools can extend expertise when they reduce routine burden, preserve context, surface patterns,

00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:26.527
or make review easier.

00:00:26.527 --> 00:00:29.096
Automation can help with consistency and speed.

00:00:29.096 --> 00:00:33.133
AI assistance can summarize, draft, compare, search, classify, or generate options.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.703
But tool output still needs expert review.

00:00:35.703 --> 00:00:39.373
A tool can produce fluent results without understanding context, consequences,

00:00:39.373 --> 00:00:41.575
or the organization's tolerance for risk.

00:00:41.575 --> 00:00:43.778
A major challenge is avoiding deskilling.

00:00:43.778 --> 00:00:46.347
If people accept tool output without inspection,

00:00:46.347 --> 00:00:50.017
they may lose the habit of checking assumptions, noticing exceptions,

00:00:50.017 --> 00:00:52.587
and understanding why an answer is appropriate.

00:00:52.587 --> 00:00:55.890
Better designs keep humans engaged in the judgment loop.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.826
They use tools to make expertise more effective,

00:00:58.826 --> 00:01:03.598
not to hide the work so completely that no one can evaluate it.

00:01:03.598 --> 00:01:08.002
Teams can make expertise reusable by capturing examples, decision records, review notes,

00:01:08.002 --> 00:01:09.470
checklists, and lessons learned.

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:13.141
They can teach expertise by explaining how strong performers think,

00:01:13.141 --> 00:01:14.976
not just what they conclude.

00:01:14.976 --> 00:01:17.545
AI-assisted work makes this even more important.

00:01:17.545 --> 00:01:21.950
The strongest teams use tools to amplify judgment, while preserving accountability, review,

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:25.620
and the ability to explain why a decision makes sense.
